# Clatter peer hosts for cross-machine discovery.
# Copy this file to  ~/.claude/clatter/peers  and list one SSH host/alias per line (the same name
# you'd pass to `ssh <host>`; # starts a comment). Then:
#   - `/clat peers` aggregates those hosts' live sessions (shown as name@host)
#   - a bare-name `/clat ask <name> ...` locates the peer across these hosts automatically
# Requires Clatter installed on each peer and working key-based (non-interactive) SSH.
#
# box
# laptop
